{
 "id": "U-06",
 "note": "U-06: the user's own patterns (secret_extra_rules HARD/WARN, prod_patterns, ticket_pattern, relaunch_allow, deny_class_patterns, and protected_branches globs that mix * and **) run in a forked child the helper kills at a wall-clock limit (lib/userre.pm). A stopped one takes its setting's safe side (a secret rule withholds, a production pattern or a protected branch counts as a match, a ticket pattern gives no ticket, a relaunch_allow or deny_class_patterns entry does not match), writes one regex_timeout {key, index, why} row and gets a /status warning; NAME globs and the other protected_branches globs compile to regexes that cannot backtrack (same answers as the plain translation). Each lib check runs in a child the runner kills after 20 s of CPU (6 times that of wall time when it waits), so code without the bound ((a+)+$ on 100 KB of a then b backtracks for minutes) fails as hung; the CLI steps have a 20 s step timeout and a time ceiling. Review round 2: the limit and the budget grow with the text (0.3 s per whole MiB, the budget up to the caller's ceiling), so a plain rule on a 10 MB file runs to the end; a run that did not finish is remembered with the text's length and its CPU, so a pattern stopped on a big file still runs on a short summary and a busy machine's stops add up; a stopped WARN rule does not stop the HARD rules after it; every pattern key, and the wait skill's marker regex, refuses a wildcard property (it runs at compile time, unbounded); setting values are trimmed in linear time; no pattern is hashed while the session has no marker. Review round 3: the watcher trims `watcher` and `handoff_turn` in linear time too; a run the budget cut short is not remembered against the pattern; ticket_pattern and the report's manifest scan have time of their own outside the budget; a load stop that leaves no time for the second try still reads load; checks guard the answer line (a long answer is not the pattern's time) and the budget ceiling. Under load (0.1.2): a budget cut stays `budget` when the helper wakes late, after the child ended by its own alarm (it read `timeout` and was remembered); whether a pattern ran is seen in the child, not read from how long a call took; upper bounds count the pattern children's time less the helper's late wake-ups, and the per-call overhead and the in-process bounds (NAME glob, trim, wildcard) count CPU; a check that wants a normal pattern run to the end runs a call again after a `load` stop in which each stopped child ran, in real time less its late wake-ups, to its own limit (the test's, grown with the text), to the start's end if it never said it was ready, or to the budget it was given, or after a first try the budget (or the ticket's own time) cut when its child started too late for its limit to end first and it ran that whole time, and fails on any other stop; a first try the budget cut passes as a busy machine (budget, load, load-no-time, ticket) only after such a measured late start; answer-not-limit judges each try by where its limit fell in the helper's own waits (the whole answer read after 1.1 times the limit passes, a stop after the D line fails, anything else moves the limit, up to 5 tries); the rows a stop writes take their pid from STORE_TEST_CLAUDE_PID, and no check lists processes with ps or pgrep.",
 "now": "2026-10-26T03:00:00+02:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-2",
 "steps": [
  {"name": "prod_patterns: a stopped pattern is production, not run again", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "prod"}},
  {"name": "prod_patterns: normal input, answers and overhead", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "prod-normal"}},
  {"name": "secret_extra_rules: a stopped rule withholds", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "secret"}},
  {"name": "secret_extra_rules: normal input, same hits and redaction", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "secret-normal"}},
  {"name": "ticket_pattern: a stopped pattern gives no ticket", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "ticket"}},
  {"name": "relaunch_allow: a stopped pattern does not allowlist", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "relaunch"}},
  {"name": "protected_branches: a stopped mixed glob protects", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "protected"}},
  {"name": "NAME glob: no backtracking", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "name-glob"}},
  {"name": "globs: the plain translation's answers", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "glob-same", "budget": 100}},
  {"name": "the process budget: later patterns take the safe side unrun", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "budget"}},
  {"name": "the budget counts all the time: twenty patterns under the limit stop when it is spent", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "total", "limit": 0.25, "budget": 0.4}},
  {"name": "a busy machine is not a slow pattern: tried once more, not marked slow; a second try cut by the budget is still load", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "load", "limit": 0.3}},
  {"name": "a slow pattern is not run again in a later process of the session", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "persist"}},
  {"name": "a busy machine: the stops of a slow pattern add up, and it is skipped once they used its limit", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "accumulate", "limit": 0.3}},
  {"name": "a plain HARD rule on a 10 MB file runs to the end; a rule stopped on a large text still runs on a short summary", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "big-linear"}},
  {"name": "secret_extra_rules: a stopped WARN rule does not stop a HARD rule after it", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "warn-then-hard"}},
  {"name": "every pattern key refuses a wildcard property (it runs while the pattern compiles)", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "wildcard"}},
  {"name": "settings: a long run of spaces inside a value is trimmed in linear time", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "trim"}},
  {"name": "no marker in the session: no pattern is hashed", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "no-hash"}},
  {"name": "ticket_pattern: its own limit whoever calls", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "ticket-limit"}},
  {"name": "a many-match WARN answer is never withheld", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "many-match", "limit": 2, "budget": 100, "cpu_share": 0.5}},
  {"name": "without Time::HiRes: a many-match WARN answer is never withheld", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "many-match", "limit": 2, "budget": 100, "cpu_share": 0.5, "no_hires": 1}},
  {"name": "without Time::HiRes: a stopped prod pattern is production within its limit", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "prod", "no_hires": 1}},
  {"name": "without Time::HiRes: the budget counts all the time", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "total", "limit": 0.25, "budget": 0.4, "no_hires": 1}},
  {"name": "the pattern child holds no lock of the helper's", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "no-lock"}},
  {"name": "the watcher's push check with only bounded protected_branches entries", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "rows-gate"}},
  {"name": "no orphan: the pattern child ends when the helper is killed or stopped", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "no-orphan"}},
  {"name": "a run the budget cut short is not remembered against the pattern", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "budget-no-mark"}},
  {"name": "ticket_pattern: time of its own, a spent budget still gives the ticket", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "ticket-own-time"}},
  {"name": "the report's manifest: its own time, a budget the files spent does not stop the rules on it", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "manifest-reserve"}},
  {"name": "a very long answer does not count against the pattern's limit", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "answer-not-limit"}},
  {"name": "the budget for a large text stops at the caller's ceiling", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "ceiling"}},
  {"name": "a load stop that leaves no time for the second try is still load", "lib": "user_regex_bound", "args": {"check": "load-no-time"}},
  {"name": "risk: a production pattern stopped at its limit asks, one row", "options": {"prod_patterns": "(a{1,30}){1,30}$"}, "env": {"STORE_TEST_CLAUDE_PID": "1:$LSTART1"}, "setup": [{"write": "$ROOT/.sessions/by-pid/1-1792580000.live-11111111.json", "content": "{\"pid\": 1, \"pid_lstart\": \"$LSTART1\", \"session_id\": \"$SID\", \"cwd\": \"$TMP\", \"worktree\": \"$TMP\", \"source\": \"startup\", \"ts\": \"2026-10-26T02:00:00+02:00\"}"}, {"write": "$TMP/cmd.txt", "content": "echo aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaab\n"}], "argv": ["risk", "--cmd-file", "$TMP/cmd.txt"], "timeout_s": 20, "expect": {"exit": 0, "ms_max": 6000, "stdout_has": ["^risk: ask \\(.*production"], "rows": [{"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "regex_timeout", "count": 1, "fields": {"key": "prod_patterns", "index": 1}}]}},
  {"name": "status: the warning line", "argv": ["status", "--sid", "$SID"], "expect": {"exit": 0, "stdout_has": ["^warning: prod_patterns #1 stopped (after its time limit|while the machine was busy); counted as production( \\(make the pattern simpler\\))?$"]}},
  {"name": "PermissionDenied: a stopped deny_class_patterns entry classes nothing, inside the 2 s hook", "options": {"deny_class_patterns": "secret=(a{1,30}){1,30}$"}, "argv": ["hook", "PermissionDenied"], "stdin_json": {"session_id": "$SID", "hook_event_name": "PermissionDenied", "tool_name": "Bash", "reason": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "tool_input": {"command": "ls"}}, "timeout_s": 20, "expect": {"exit": 0, "ms_max": 1900, "rows": [{"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "permission_denied", "count": 1, "fields": {"guard_class": "other"}}, {"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "regex_timeout", "count": 1, "fields": {"key": "deny_class_patterns", "index": 1}}]}},
  {"name": "PermissionDenied: twenty deny_class_patterns that each finish under the limit stay inside the 2 s hook", "options": {"deny_class_patterns": "secret=(a+)+(?#1)$;secret=(a+)+(?#2)$;secret=(a+)+(?#3)$;secret=(a+)+(?#4)$;secret=(a+)+(?#5)$;secret=(a+)+(?#6)$;secret=(a+)+(?#7)$;secret=(a+)+(?#8)$;secret=(a+)+(?#9)$;secret=(a+)+(?#10)$;secret=(a+)+(?#11)$;secret=(a+)+(?#12)$;secret=(a+)+(?#13)$;secret=(a+)+(?#14)$;secret=(a+)+(?#15)$;secret=(a+)+(?#16)$;secret=(a+)+(?#17)$;secret=(a+)+(?#18)$;secret=(a+)+(?#19)$;secret=(a+)+(?#20)$"}, "argv": ["hook", "PermissionDenied"], "stdin_json": {"session_id": "$SID", "hook_event_name": "PermissionDenied", "tool_name": "Bash", "reason": "", "tool_input": {"command": "ls"}}, "timeout_s": 20, "expect": {"exit": 0, "ms_max": 1900, "rows": [{"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "permission_denied", "count": 2}, {"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "regex_timeout", "fields": {"key": "deny_class_patterns", "index": 20, "why": "budget"}}]}},
  {"name": "PermissionDenied: deny_class_patterns past 32 entries or 200 characters are not used", "options": {"deny_class_patterns": "routing=zzz(?#1);routing=zzz(?#2);routing=zzz(?#3);routing=zzz(?#4);routing=zzz(?#5);routing=zzz(?#6);routing=zzz(?#7);routing=zzz(?#8);routing=zzz(?#9);routing=zzz(?#10);routing=zzz(?#11);routing=zzz(?#12);routing=zzz(?#13);routing=zzz(?#14);routing=zzz(?#15);routing=zzz(?#16);routing=zzz(?#17);routing=zzz(?#18);routing=zzz(?#19);routing=zzz(?#20);routing=zzz(?#21);routing=zzz(?#22);routing=zzz(?#23);routing=zzz(?#24);routing=zzz(?#25);routing=zzz(?#26);routing=zzz(?#27);routing=zzz(?#28);routing=zzz(?#29);routing=zzz(?#30);routing=zzz(?#31);routing=zzz(?#32);scope=ls"}, "argv": ["hook", "PermissionDenied"], "stdin_json": {"session_id": "$SID", "hook_event_name": "PermissionDenied", "tool_name": "Bash", "reason": "no", "tool_input": {"command": "ls"}}, "expect": {"exit": 0, "rows": [{"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "permission_denied", "count": 3}, {"file": "$WATCH/$SID.classic.jsonl", "ev": "permission_denied", "count": 0, "fields": {"guard_class": "scope"}}]}},
